[N 39-40 The Tempest's Weapons]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Home from Kalimdor by Booty Bay: Seahorn's gem, Veyric and the Eye of the Tempest, the last of Faldir's Cove, Rage of the Storm from Bath'rah, then the Syndicate in Alterac - Dark Council, Baron Vardus and the Ensorcelled Parchment - the Coldbringer's Eye to Lan'dalock, Scarlet Monastery's Cathedral for In the Name of the Light, and Stormpike in Ironforge.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 39: Nagaz and Baron Vardus are 40, the Ruins' Enforcers 39-40, the cove naga 38-40. The Cathedral of Scarlet Monastery (mobs 37-42, Mograine and Whitemane 42 elite) wants a full group of five at 39-40. Under 39: the Alterac kills are slower - bring a friend for Nagaz and the Baron, or carry Dark Council (537) and Baron's Demise (523) to the next pass through Southshore
[OC]|cffffffffThe Tempest's Weapons|r  -  you start at the Razorfen Downs door by Myriam Moonsinger where chapter 39b left you; hearth = Farholde Keep and it is not used here (the chapter ends in Ironforge). About 36,890 quest XP and 3g 05s are handed in here, every quest plain: Ratchet and the boat to Booty Bay, a flight to Refuge Pointe, Veyric and Faldir's Cove, Southshore, the Alterac loop (Bath'rah, Strahnbrad, the Ruins, the Dalaran crater), the swim to Scarlet Monastery's Cathedral (|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r) and back, Southshore again, then Ironforge
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Sunken Treasure (669) with the Sample Elven Gem from the cove (chapter 39); shaman: Heed My Call (96135) with the Eye of the Tempest (the ritual, chapter 39); The Coldbringer's Eye (96773, from chapter 34, the Eye looted in Razorfen Downs); In the Name of the Light (1053, from chapter 34: Loksey and Herod done, Mograine and Whitemane open) and The Scarlet Key from Doan's Strongbox. Bring the Light (3636) rides to chapter 39d if you took it. Maleb offers Dark Council since chapter 27 (Further Mysteries, 525)
